Take the KF version from the style that has KDE support

The QTC_INSTALL_PO block selects a KF major version. The block then
requires the I18n component of that version. Two separate if() blocks
make the choice. The Qt 6 block sets 6, and the Qt 5 block sets 5. The
Qt 5 block runs last, so a build with both Qt versions selects KF5.

Such a build then needs the KF5 I18n framework. The Qt 5 style finds
KF5 only when QTC_QT5_ENABLE_KDE is on. A build with that option off
therefore needs KF5 for the translation files alone.

Make the choice an if/elseif chain, and test the KDE support of each
style first. A style that has KDE support finds its own KF version
with the I18n component. The translation files then need no further
framework.

Each KDE test also keeps its ENABLE_QT option. A KDE option can stay on
when the build drops its style. qt5/CMakeLists.txt can turn ENABLE_QT5
off when it does not find Qt 5. The same file turns QTC_QT5_ENABLE_KDE
off in its own scope alone, so that option stays on in this block.

The chain takes KF6 only where the Qt 6 style has KDE support, or
where no style has KDE support. The upstream default build keeps KF5,
because it builds the Qt 5 style with KDE support. A build with KDE 6
support and no KDE 5 support selects KF6, and needs no KF5. A build
with no KDE support follows the two Qt options, where Qt 6 now comes
before Qt 5. Such a build with both Qt versions moves from KF5 to KF6.

Drop this patch when upstream takes the KF version from the style
that has KDE support.

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index 66e2dbfe..347c7c90 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -253,10 +253,17 @@ if(QTC_INSTALL_PO)
   find_package(ECM 1.2.0 REQUIRED NO_MODULE)
   set(CMAKE_MODULE_PATH ${CMAKE_MODULE_PATH} ${ECM_MODULE_PATH})
 
-  if (ENABLE_QT6)
+  # Take a framework version that the build already needs. A style that
+  # has KDE support finds its own KF version and the I18n component.
+  # Each KDE branch also tests its ENABLE_QT option, because
+  # qt5/CMakeLists.txt can turn ENABLE_QT5 off when it does not find Qt 5.
+  if (ENABLE_QT6 AND QTC_QT6_ENABLE_KDE)
     set(KF_MAJOR_VERSION 6)
-  endif()
-  if (ENABLE_QT5)
+  elseif (ENABLE_QT5 AND QTC_QT5_ENABLE_KDE)
+    set(KF_MAJOR_VERSION 5)
+  elseif (ENABLE_QT6)
+    set(KF_MAJOR_VERSION 6)
+  elseif (ENABLE_QT5)
     set(KF_MAJOR_VERSION 5)
   endif()
   find_package(KF${KF_MAJOR_VERSION} REQUIRED COMPONENTS
